## Cross-links & boundaries

- **`caching`** here is application/distributed caching only (Redis/Memcached, CDN, cache-aside, eviction, invalidation). CPU/hardware cache lines belong to Area 5's `caches`; DB-internal buffer-pool/query-cache belongs to Area 2's `storage-indexing`. Don't re-teach those here — reference them.
- **`api-design`** stays inside System Design (per the map's overlap flag) rather than becoming its own Area.
- **`observability`** here is the HLD/interview view — what to instrument, SLI/SLO as a design input, tracing across a design's own services. Hands-on tooling and ops runbooks belong to Area 10's `observability-ops`; boundary note is inlined above the group.
- **`sd-playbook`** is the canonical home for the interview method; Area 17's `sd-interview-playbook` is the same group by another name and should point here, not duplicate.
- Within the area: `resilience/rate-limiting-algorithms` is the one canonical home for limiter algorithms — `case-studies` intentionally has no separate "design a rate limiter" topic. `messaging-streaming/message-delivery-semantics` (idempotency) is referenced from `resilience/retries-timeouts-and-backoff` and `api-design/api-design-deep-practices` rather than re-derived. `consistency-replication/conflict-resolution` (CRDTs) is referenced from `case-studies/design-collaborative-editor` rather than re-derived. `storage-scale`'s shard-key and hotspot material is referenced from `case-studies/design-news-feed` and `design-proximity-service` rather than repeated.
- **Flagged gaps (not included, for reviewer to weigh in):** no dedicated topic for a distributed lock/coordination service (e.g. ZooKeeper/etcd) beyond the passing mention in `consistency-replication/consensus-basics` — could warrant its own topic or case study. No file-sync/"design Google Drive/Dropbox" case study — `storage-scale/object-and-blob-storage` covers the storage half but not multi-device sync/conflict handling at the case-study level.
